## Scoped long-path correction

The retained `actual-start-02-preflight-failure.json` records the original-parent-blob check failing inside preflight before project imports. The principal finding records the intact 264-character logical path, 7,473 exact bytes, expected content hash, regular non-reparse metadata, and absent fresh roots. That evidence supports correcting filesystem spelling without changing the artifact or its authority.

The Windows conversion follows the existing convention in `core/pit_optimizer_artifacts.py:482-488`: retain an existing extended prefix, convert UNC spelling to the extended UNC form, and prefix the absolute drive path otherwise. Conversion occurs at filesystem-call boundaries; logical Path values remain the inputs to native repositories, resource/tool identities, containment checks, relative refs, and reports. None of the original dependency refs, expected hashes, native preparation/config/owner inputs, policy/caps, or renderer arguments changed.

The complete fix diff and necessary native convention were reviewed. Exact reads now use extended-path lstat/open/fstat, require regular non-link/non-reparse files, compare device/inode across opening and reading, and retain the original content-hash comparison. Alias inspection remains lstat-only and still makes no alias content-hash claim. Directory validation walks the logical absolute components and rejects link/reparse entries before returning the unprefixed logical path.

Fresh-root creation, directory enumeration, existence checks, destination parent creation, and exclusive writes now use extended disk paths. O_CREAT/O_EXCL, full write/fsync/close handling, existing-root rejection, logical containment checks, and fresh-root emptiness checks remain. The added parent and post-write regular-file checks preserve fail-closed behavior; no overwrite, truncation, rename, deletion, or missing-file bypass is introduced.

Snapshot traversal now explicitly enumerates every directory with extended-path scandir, recurses into directories, hashes regular files through the guarded reader, and rejects links/reparse points and other non-regular entries. Keys remain sorted logical relative paths. Thus long files remain covered by both before/after snapshots instead of being silently omitted. Source and readiness checks use the same exact reader. The fixed principal finding is authenticated by the existing pre-import review gate.

AST inspection found only the filesystem helpers, their callers, and finding/report additions shown in the scoped diff; no function was removed. The corrected driver parses as an AST. No new finding arose. Earlier import fixes, truthful environment reporting, launcher/native-interpreter distinction, source/readiness gates, exact import inventory, native fresh preparation, preview-only request construction, and absence of operational invocation remain supported by the retained reviews and unchanged portions.

